Z||000000||JohnsFiero||08-27-2000||12:53 AM||||My '84 has a plaque on the shifter console regarding the fiero and engine fires because of lack of regular maintenance.  Have never seen one of these before.  Should I keep it or toss it?  Was it standard or after the recalls?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||08-27-2000||02:30 AM||||That plaque was part of the engine fire recall.  You are the first one I've heard of that actually has the plaque installed on the car.  When I picked up my 84 after the recall (99,600 miles and a FREE engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">), the service manager handed me the plaque and said I could stick it on if I wanted to.  I think I still have stashed around here somewhere.<p>[This message has been edited by Rodrv6 (edited 08-27-2000).]||||reg||7
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||08-27-2000||09:04 AM||||I still have my plaque too. I never took the plastic cover off it.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg">  <B>My 1985 2M4 Sport Coupe </B><P><BR><B>My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A></B>||||reg||14
Z||000003||theogre||08-27-2000||02:17 PM||||No plaque but I did run across a copy of the little book that I think all the recall repaired cars where suposed to get. They are year specific.||||reg||1
